Package: causalpanelfusion
Title: Causal Data Fusion for Panel Data without a Pre-Intervention Period
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zou", "Yang", email = "zou.yang.th@dartmouth.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Seung Hee", "Lee", email = "seunghee@bu.edu", role = "aut"))
Description: Estimates the causal effect of an intervention on a single
    treated unit when the target domain has no pre-intervention period, by
    fusing panel data from a related reference domain observed for the same
    units (Yang, Lee, Kohler and Ghassami, <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2410.16391>).
    Implements synthetic control data fusion with data-driven constrained
    weights, linear and logarithmic equi-confounding estimators, prediction
    intervals that combine a bootstrap for the weight-construction error with
    donor-placebo calibration of the transfer error, per-period prediction
    bands, placebo and RMSPE-ratio tests, and sensitivity analyses. The
    optimisation uses the free 'ECOS' conic solver by default; 'Gurobi' is
    supported as an option.
